# PonyAI — Quantitative Trading Platform

A modular quantitative trading system model built in Python.

## Architecture

```
ponyai/
├── data/       # DataFeed with SHA-256 integrity verification
├── strategy/   # Abstract Strategy base class
├── broker/     # PaperBroker, Portfolio, Fill (with PnL tracking)
├── backtest/   # BacktestEngine orchestrating data → strategy → broker
├── risk/       # Performance metrics (Sharpe, drawdown, Calmar, …)
└── deploy/     # CanaryRouter for gradual strategy roll-out
```

## Quick Start

```bash
# Install in development mode
pip install -e ".[dev]"

# Run tests
pytest
```

## Modules

| Module | Key Classes | Purpose |
|--------|------------|---------|
| `data` | `DataFeed` | Load CSV/Parquet data with SHA-256 checksum versioning |
| `strategy` | `Strategy` (ABC), `Signal` | Define trading logic via `on_bar` / `on_init` / `on_finish` |
| `broker` | `PaperBroker`, `Portfolio`, `Fill` | Simulated execution, position & cash tracking |
| `backtest` | `BacktestEngine`, `BacktestResult` | Run strategy over historical data, collect equity curve |
| `risk` | `compute_metrics` | Sharpe ratio, max drawdown, annual return, Calmar ratio |
| `deploy` | `CanaryRouter` | A/B-style gradual deployment of new strategies |
